(vector (map (:adr/id "adr-2607072100-kotoba-server-fleet-deployment-strangler-fig")
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/title "kotoba-server fleet deployment & strangler-fig strategy: staged rollout (Month 1–3)")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-07-20")
  (:adr/owner-instruction "plan staged cljc mesh node deployment to murakumo fleet: parallel run, parity validation, traffic migration with rollback triggers")
  (:db/id -1)

  (:adr/body "# ADR-2607072100: kotoba-server fleet deployment & strangler-fig strategy: staged rollout (Month 1–3)\n\n**Status**: accepted (deployment roadmap & parity/performance/rollback decision framework)\n**Date**: 2026-07-20\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki（指示: cljc mesh node の本番 fleet 展開計画と段階的カットオーバー手順）\n**Scope**: `orgs/murakumo-family/murakumo`（fleet orchestration、staging 環境の新設）、\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/{kototama,kotoba,mesh_node_deployments}`（cljc node implementation）、\nMonth 1–3 の parallel-run & traffic-migration タイムライン\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2607072000 が「Rust が必要な実装は全て cljc」の標準方針を確立し、\nkotoba-server を最優先ギャップとして名指しした。ADR-2607082400 が\n実機検証で2つの壁（component model・gossipsub）を確定した上で、\nstrangler-fig パターン（既存 Rust fleet は無変更、新規容量を cljc で構築）\nという現実的な方向を示した。同 ADR の3つの follow-up（drama-profile の\n`.kotoba` 移植、HTTP 契約設計、kgraph capability 採用）はすべて実装完了済み\n（2026-07-08）。\n\n本 ADR は、この技術的な基盤の上で、**実際に cljc mesh node を本番 murakumo\nfleet（Mac-mini 群）へ段階的に展開する**ための deployment roadmap、\nparity validation checklist、performance budgets、rollback triggers を決める。\n本番影響が大きいため、month-by-month timeline を明示し、exit criteria と\nroll-back clause を明記する。\n\n### 前提条件（確定事項）\n\n1. **既存 fleet・既存 mesh app（minidrama/kenchi/kotodama-bot）は Rust\n   kotoba-server のままで変更しない**（ADR-2607082400 §2）。新規容量のため\n   の新 node として cljc を追加する strawman パターン。\n\n2. **coordination axis は murakumo 主導**（ADR-2607071900 で既に\n   cross-node auction を murakumo の cljc control-plane だけで実装）。\n   gossipsub による peer discovery / mesh maintenance を新規実装しない —\n   既存の centralized fleet.edn management を踏襲する。\n\n3. **guest 言語は `.kotoba`、既存 component 再利用ではなく新規移植判定**\n   （ADR-2607082400 follow-up ①）。ただし Month 1–3 では drama-profile\n   のみを対象にし、他の app（valuation-query/ingest/reply など）は\n   後続の phase に遅延させる。\n\n4. **HTTP contract は `GET /health` + `POST /mesh/http/<route>`**\n   （ADR-2607082400 follow-up ③）。kotoba-server と同じ URL 形状。murakumo\n   からの `PUT /fleet/<node>/routes/<name>` で route を登録。\n\n## Decision\n\n### Phase 1: Staging & Parallel-Run（Month 1, Week 1–4）\n\n#### 1.1 Staging 環境の構築\n\n- **新 cljc mesh node の初期 cluster**: murakumo fleet の **1/3 サブセット**\n  （既存: 9 nodes、新: 3 nodes cljc。同じ Mac-mini hardware 仕様）。\n- **network isolation**: staging 用 gossipsub topic / IPFS DHT pin set を\n  fleet.edn に新規追加（既存 Rust fleet と peer-neighbor しない、pure\n  segregation）。\n- **murakumo control plane**: staging pool の node list を `manifest/fleet-db.edn`\n  に `:fleet/nodes` entry で登録。`GET /fleet/nodes?pool=staging` で staging\n  node リスト取得可能にする。\n- **single-app deployment（drama-profile only）**: 他 app（kenchi/minidrama\n  の valuation/ingest など）は staging 期間中は未登録のままにする —\n  HTTP `404 :not-bound-route` を返す。\n\n#### 1.2 Parity Validation Setup（Month 1, Week 1–2）\n\nmurakumo の `metrics-ingest` に新しい metrics を追加：\n\n- **Per-route latency (HTTP POST)**: p50/p95/p99 + percentile histogram\n  （rust-node vs cljc-node で同じ metric name、`node_runtime` tag で\n  区別）。\n- **Per-route throughput**: req/sec (moving avg over 5min window)。\n- **Memory usage (instance)**: JVM heap size (Xmx baseline + observed peak)。\n- **Instance creation latency**: Chicory compile → instantiate → first\n  export call (p95)。\n- **Parity assertions**: (a) \"`drama-profile` HTTP POST で identical JSON\n  response を両 runtime から取得」, (b)「same input の assert/query で\n  同一 datom が観測」（content-hash comparison）, (c)「HTTP status code\n  identity」（both 200 or both 400, not divergent）。\n\nAutomated parity checker (`murakumo/parity-checker.cljs`, nbb):\n- Staging pool の各 cljc node へ HTTP request を送信。\n- 同じ request を routing layer で Rust node pool にも送信。\n- Response を byte-by-byte / semantic equality で比較。\n- Divergence を見つけたら murakumo metrics に `:parity-fail: true` を\n  記録 && alert を上げる。\n\n#### 1.3 Parallel-Run Traffic Pattern（Month 1, Week 2–4）\n\n- murakumo の route-dispatch layer：staging pool へ **5% of\n  drama-profile requests**（canary）を送信。残り95% は既存 Rust pool へ。\n- parity checker は全 request に対して走行（5% canary + 95% baseline\n  sample の両方をドレーン）。\n- **SLO target during staging**: p99 latency ≤ 150ms（Rust baseline +\n  50ms overhead 容認）、parity failure ≤ 0.01%（99.99% pass）、memory\n  usage ≤ 256MB per instance。\n- **staging duration**: 2週間を minimum baseline。metrics が安定に達した\n  時点で phase 2 へ進行判定を行う（日次 review + owner approval）。\n\n### Phase 2: Parity Validation & Traffic Ramp（Month 2, Week 1–4）\n\n#### 2.1 Parity Validation Checkpoint（Month 2, Week 1）\n\nStaging 期間中の metrics 分析：\n\n- **Parity checklist**: 上記 (a)/(b)/(c) のすべてが pass。divergence found\n  → stage return to Phase 1 debugging, or abort if critical path broken。\n- **Performance baseline**: p95 latency ≤ 100ms（50ms buffer margin）、\n  throughput loss < 5%、heap stability without GC pause spikes > 100ms。\n- **Reliability**: crash / panic / unhandled exception なし。HTTP 500\n  rate ≤ 0.01%。\n- **Audit trail**: 全 request/response のログを blob store に rotate\n  （Backblaze B2 + DataLad、容量計画: 2 weeks × 5% traffic ≈ 100GB）。\n\n**Validation threshold exceeded**: いずれかの項目が threshold を超えた場合\n→ 原因分析に立ち戻る。修正が小（single-component fix）なら staging\n継続。修正が大（architecture change）なら current cljc node を全削除\nして ADR-2607082400 の後続 phase に遅延。\n\n#### 2.2 Traffic Ramp-Up（Month 2, Week 2–4）\n\nParity validation が pass したら、canary traffic を段階的に増加：\n\n- **Week 2**: 5% → 10% （cljc pool へ new node 追加なし、既存 3 node で\n  throughput increase absorb）。\n- **Week 3**: 10% → 25% （容量不足なら new node deploy, pool size up to 6）。\n- **Week 4**: 25% → 50% （balanced load, pool size ≥ 6）。\n\n各 step で 3 日間の stability window を設ける —— metrics が stable なら\nnext step へ、divergence / performance regression / reliability issue なら\nstep を revert（traffic down, root-cause analysis, fix, re-test）。\n\n**SLO during ramp**:\n- p99 latency: baseline + 50ms（ramp 中の GC 等による transient増加を許容）。\n- throughput: loss なし（ただし p95 は +10% acceptable）。\n- memory: per-instance ≤ 384MB（peak）。\n- parity: ≤ 0.05% failure rate（canary traffic の signal/noise ratio）。\n- reliability: HTTP 5xx ≤ 0.1%。\n\n### Phase 3: Cutover & Stabilization（Month 3, Week 1–2）\n\n#### 3.1 Final Validation（Month 3, Week 1）\n\nMonth 2 end に 50% traffic に達した状態で、1 week の stability sentinel を置く：\n\n- All metrics within SLO.\n- Parity failure rate < 0.01%（production-ready threshold）.\n- No panics / crashes / unhandled exceptions.\n- Alert noise < 2 per day（false positive）.\n\n**Go/No-Go decision gate**: owner + ops review の上、cutover 継行 or\nabort を決定。abort の場合は current cljc pool を shrink して staging\nに戻し、issues を fix してから再スケジュール。\n\n#### 3.2 Traffic Migration（Month 3, Week 1–2）\n\nGo decision が出たら、final ramp:\n\n- 50% → 75% → 90% → 99%（Rust pool の SLA degradation monitor 付き）。\n- **最後の 1% は explicit cutover**: 既存 Rust node を DNS unhealthy 化\n  （health check 偽陰性）→ client-side retry で cljc pool へ自動 fallback。\n  Rust node は graceful shutdown まで留置（old request の tail-latency\n  absorb 用）。\n\n**Timeline**: 50% → 99% の ramp は 3 日以上を要する（各 step での\nmetrics stabilization window）。最終的に 100% は implicit（Rust pool の\ngraceful drain を完了）。\n\n#### 3.3 Rollback Triggers（Month 3, Week 2）\n\n**自動 rollback 条件**（autonomous trigger、owner confirmation なし）：\n\n1. **Latency regression**: p99 > baseline + 100ms sustained for > 5 min\n   → cljc traffic fraction を前の safe state に revert。\n2. **Parity failure**: divergence rate > 1% sustained for > 1 min → full\n   revert（traffic 100% back to Rust）。\n3. **Reliability**: HTTP 5xx rate > 1% sustained for > 2 min → full revert。\n4. **New unrecovered exception**: panic / crash / SIGSEGV を observe → full\n   revert + debug session on staging pool。\n5. **Capacity exhaustion**: observed memory > 512MB per instance sustained\n   → revert + node pool size increase + re-test。\n\n**Manual rollback triggers**（owner decision）：\n- Parity violation で root cause が application-level（e.g., kgraph query\n  semantics mismatch）→ app fix → re-test（full Rust revert なし、staging\n  に戻して修正）。\n- Performance budget miss（e.g., expected p99 140ms, actual 160ms）で許容\n  range — acceptable for another month of optimization → continue (SLO\n  escalation, not revert).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) 段階的 month-by-month timeline により、各 phase で本番影響を\n  最小化しながら parity & performance を實證できる（failure point を\n  早期に catch）。\n- (+) Parity checklist & performance budget & rollback triggers を明文化\n  することで、deployment decision の客観性と audit trail を確保。\n- (+) Staging pool（3 nodes）の segregation により、既存 Rust fleet\n  （9 nodes）への immediate blast radius がゼロ。\n- (+) Traffic canary（5% → 25% → 50% → 99%）により、issue discovery を\n  incremental にでき、1 回の full 本番切替時に初めて顕在化する\n  pathological case を最小化。\n- (−) Month 1–3 のタイムライン中に既存 mesh app（kenchi valuation /\n  minidrama component 群）は Rust のままで、「strangler-fig の新規容量」\n  は drama-profile のみに限定される —— phase 3 stable period に他の app\n  の移植を検討する（本 ADR では範囲外）。\n- (−) JVM GC pause（especially stop-the-world generational GC）が予期せず\n  large（>100ms）になる risk があり、その場合 p99 latency budget を\n  breech する可能性 —— mitigation は `jvm.options` での GC tuning\n  （ZGC / Shenandoah evaluation）を month 2 中に evaluate する（本 ADR\n  の追加 action item）。\n\n## Architecture Diagram（ASCII diagram 備考）\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     murakumo control-plane                    │\n│                   (fleet.edn management)                      │\n│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ fleet-db.edn: nodes=Rust(pool-prod 9x) + cljc(staging) │  │\n│  │ parity-checker: canary-route={drama-profile,…}         │  │\n│  │ metrics-ingest: latency/throughput/memory/parity       │  │\n│  │ route-dispatch: traffic-split 5% → 99% (cljc%)         │  │\n│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n         ↓ HTTP PUT /fleet/<node>/routes/<route>         \n         ↓ HTTP GET /fleet/nodes?pool=staging\n         │                                                     \n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Rust kotoba-server pool (production, 9 nodes, no change)      │\n│ ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ gossipsub mesh (cross-node auction lattice running)      │ │\n│ │ - minidrama: drama-profile, drama-heartbeat             │ │\n│ │ - kenchi: valuation-query, valuation-refresh            │ │\n│ │ - kotodama-bot: ingest, reply                           │ │\n│ │ [not touched by this ADR]                               │ │\n│ └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n         ↑ respond to canary requests (95%)\n         │ (parity-checker compares responses)\n         │\n         ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n         │ cljc mesh node cluster (staging, 3–6 nodes added)  │\n         │ ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n         │ │ Chicory wasm runtime (JVM kototama.tender)  │   │\n         │ │ .kotoba guest: drama-profile (phase 1 only)  │   │\n         │ │ Route dispatch: GET /health, POST /mesh/http/│   │\n         │ │   drama-profile                              │   │\n         │ │ kgraph-assert!/kgraph-query capability      │   │\n         │ └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n         │ Metrics exported: latency/throughput/memory        │\n         └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n         ↑ respond to canary requests (5% → 99%)\n         │ (traffic ramp phase)\n         │\n         [Phase 1]: 5% traffic canary + parity validation\n         [Phase 2]: 5% → 50% incremental traffic ramp\n         [Phase 3]: 50% → 99% final migration + graceful Rust drain\n```\n\n## Parity Checklist（deployment gate）\n\n### Phase 1 Completion Criteria（end of Month 1, Week 4）\n\n- [ ] Staging pool 3 nodes: all healthy, JVM startup < 15 sec each\n- [ ] drama-profile component: compile → emit (WASM) → load in Chicory\n  ✓ test case: `test/kotoba/mesh_drama_profile_test.clj` green\n- [ ] HTTP contract: GET /health + POST /mesh/http/drama-profile\n  ✓ test case: `test/kotoba/mesh_node_test.clj` green\n- [ ] Canary traffic 5%: parity pass rate ≥ 99.99% (≤0.01% divergence)\n- [ ] Latency: p99 ≤ 150ms（Rust baseline ~100ms + 50ms overhead）\n- [ ] Throughput: no loss vs baseline\n- [ ] Memory: per-instance ≤ 256MB stable (not approaching 512MB limit)\n- [ ] Reliability: no crash / panic / 5xx rate ≤ 0.01%\n- [ ] Audit trail: request/response logs captured (B2 rotation)\n\n### Phase 2 Completion Criteria（end of Month 2, Week 4）\n\n- [ ] Traffic ramp: 5% → 50% successful, SLO maintained at each step\n- [ ] Parity failure rate: ≤ 0.05% (canary 50% window)\n- [ ] Latency sustained: p99 ≤ 100ms（optimized baseline）\n- [ ] Node pool: capacity sufficient (≥6 nodes for 50% load)\n- [ ] Alerts noise: < 5 per day false positives\n- [ ] GC tuning: tested ZGC / Shenandoah, baseline selected\n\n### Phase 3 Completion Criteria（end of Month 3, Week 2）\n\n- [ ] Final validation: 50% traffic stable for 1 week\n  - All metrics within SLO\n  - Parity < 0.01%\n  - No panics / crashes\n  - Alert noise < 2 per day\n- [ ] Traffic migration: 50% → 99% ramp completed\n- [ ] Rust pool graceful drain: old requests timed out, no 5xx\n- [ ] 100% cutover: cljc pool handles 100%, Rust pool shutdown\n\n## Performance Budgets\n\n| Metric | Phase 1 Target | Phase 2 Target | Phase 3 Target | Note |\n|--------|---|---|---|---|\n| p50 latency (ms) | ≤80 | ≤70 | ≤70 | baseline ~60ms |\n| p95 latency (ms) | ≤120 | ≤95 | ≤95 | accept 5% variance in ramp |\n| p99 latency (ms) | ≤150 | ≤100 | ≤100 | hard budget |\n| throughput loss (%) | ≤2 | ≤1 | ≤0 | vs Rust baseline |\n| JVM heap peak (MB) | ≤256 | ≤384 | ≤256 | post-GC stable |\n| GC pause p99 (ms) | ≤50 | ≤30 | ≤30 | ZGC / Shenandoah |\n| Memory leak detection | pass | pass | pass | 4-week heap profile |\n| Parity failure rate (%) | ≤0.01 | ≤0.05 | ≤0.01 | content-hash mismatch |\n| HTTP 5xx rate (%) | ≤0.01 | ≤0.1 | ≤0.01 | unhandled exceptions |\n| Instance compile time (ms) | ≤500 | ≤300 | ≤300 | Chicory → ready to serve |\n\n## Rollback Procedure\n\n### Automatic Rollback（autonomous，no owner confirmation）\n\n```clj\n(defn- should-auto-rollback? [{:keys [latency-p99 parity-fail-rate http-5xx-rate memory-peak] :as metrics}]\n  (or (and (> latency-p99 (+ baseline-p99 100))\n           (sustained-for metrics :duration-ms 300000))\n      (and (> parity-fail-rate 0.01)\n           (sustained-for metrics :duration-ms 60000))\n      (and (> http-5xx-rate 0.01)\n           (sustained-for metrics :duration-ms 120000))\n      (> memory-peak 512)))\n\n(defn rollback [to-state]\n  ;; to-state: :phase-1, :phase-2, :phase-3-previous-step, or :full-rust\n  (murakumo/set-traffic-split {:cljc-percent (get-pct to-state)})\n  (alert-ops :severity :warning :msg (str \"Auto-rollback to \" to-state))\n  (log-audit {:action :rollback :from :current :to to-state :trigger metrics}))\n```\n\n### Manual Rollback（owner decision）\n\nOwner は任意の phase で、以下の理由で rollback / abort を decide できる：\n- Application-level parity violation で quick fix が不可能\n- Performance budget miss が許容範囲（SLO escalation で continue も可）\n- Business priority change（他 app の緊急移植が必要）\n\nRollback 時の状態復帰：\n- Traffic revert: `murakumo/set-traffic-split {:cljc-percent 0}`（full Rust）\n- Nodes drain: graceful shutdown （in-flight request timeout 30sec）\n- Rust pool restore: health-check resume\n- Audit log: rollback trigger / timing / owner approval を記録\n\n## Follow-up Actions（out of scope, Month 3+ follow-up）\n\n1. **Other mesh app migration**: kenchi (valuation-query/refresh), minidrama\n   (component 群), kotodama-bot (ingest/reply) の `.kotoba` 移植。\n   各 app ごとに parity validation → deployment schedule を決める。\n\n2. **GC optimization**: ZGC / Shenandoah tuning（month 2 evaluation 結果\n   に基づき）。Large pause elimination for p99 budget compliance。\n\n3. **Gossipsub upgrade（optional）**: cljc side に peer-to-peer mesh を\n   追加する場合は、新規 ADR + full libp2p-gossipsub implementation。\n   Month 3 phase 3 complete まで遅延。\n\n4. **Staging pool permanent shutdown**: phase 3 complete 後、staging\n   segregation を撤去。cljc nodes を production fleet に統合\n   （gossipsub 再度統合、full mesh 復帰）。\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607072000（Rust 回避の標準方針 + kotoba-server 未着手の名指し）:\n  本 ADR が deployment 計画を立てるための foundation。\n- ADR-2607082400（component model / gossipsub の壁実証 + strangler-fig\n  方向性）: 本 ADR の技術的な前提（drop-in置換不可能 → staged rollout）。\n- ADR-2607071900（murakumo cross-node apply, cljc-only）:\n  centralized coordination authority としての murakumo の実証例。\n- ADR-2607062330（kototama-tender-chicory-execution-runtime）: WASM\n  guest 実行層。本 ADR のクリティカルパス。\n\n")

  (:adr/decision "{:phase-1-staging \"新cljcノード3個をstagingプール化。drama-profileのみ対象。canary 5%traffic。parity checker自動検証。SLO: p99≤150ms, parity≤0.01%, memory≤256MB\", :phase-2-ramp \"traffic 5%→50%段階的増加。各stepで3日stability window。SLO: p99≤100ms, throughput loss<5%, parity≤0.05%. GC tuning evaluation.\", :phase-3-cutover \"traffic 50%→99%→100%最終移行。rollback triggers実装（latency regression>100ms, parity>1%, 5xx>1%, memory>512MB）。owner approval gate week 1, traffic migration week 1-2.\", :existing-fleet-unchanged \"minidrama/kenchi/kotodama-botはRustのまま（ゼロリスク）。月3終了後に他appの移植検討\"}")

  (:adr/month-by-month-timeline "{:month-1 {:week \"1-2\" :action \"staging環境構築、parity checker実装、SLO baseline確定\"} {:week \"2-4\" :action \"parallel-run 5% canary、parity validation、metrics stable化\"} :month-2 {:week \"1\" :action \"parity checkpoint。threshold exceed時はphase-1に立ち戻り\"} {:week \"2-4\" :action \"traffic ramp 5%→50%。各stepで3日window。GC tuning evaluation\"} :month-3 {:week \"1\" :action \"final validation (1week sentinel)。go/no-go decision gate\"} {:week \"1-2\" :action \"traffic migration 50%→99%→100%。rollback triggers監視。graceful Rust drain\"}}")

  (:adr/rollback-triggers "{:automatic [{:trigger \"p99 latency > baseline+100ms sustained 5min\" :action \"revert to previous safe traffic state\"} {:trigger \"parity divergence > 1% sustained 1min\" :action \"full revert to Rust (100%)\"} {:trigger \"HTTP 5xx rate > 1% sustained 2min\" :action \"full revert to Rust\"} {:trigger \"memory peak > 512MB sustained\" :action \"revert + increase node pool size + retest\"}] :manual [{:trigger \"application-level parity fix needed\" :action \"staging fixcycle, staging retest, continue\"} {:trigger \"performance budget miss (acceptable range)\" :action \"escalate SLO, not revert\"}]}")

  (:adr/parity-checklist-phase-1 (vector (map (:item "staging pool 3 nodes healthy, JVM startup <15sec")) (map (:item "drama-profile component compile→emit→Chicory load")) (map (:item "HTTP GET /health + POST /mesh/http/drama-profile working")) (map (:item "canary 5% parity pass ≥99.99% (≤0.01% divergence)")) (map (:item "latency p99 ≤150ms (baseline+50ms)")) (map (:item "throughput no loss vs baseline")) (map (:item "memory per-instance ≤256MB stable")) (map (:item "reliability no crash/panic, 5xx ≤0.01%")) (map (:item "audit trail request/response captured (B2)"))))

  (:adr/parity-checklist-phase-2 (vector (map (:item "traffic ramp 5%→50% SLO maintained")) (map (:item "parity failure ≤0.05% (canary 50%)")) (map (:item "latency p99 ≤100ms sustained")) (map (:item "node pool ≥6 nodes for 50% load")) (map (:item "alert noise <5/day false positives")) (map (:item "GC tuning ZGC/Shenandoah evaluated"))))

  (:adr/parity-checklist-phase-3 (vector (map (:item "final validation 50% traffic 1week stable")) (map (:item "all metrics within SLO")) (map (:item "parity <0.01%")) (map (:item "no panics/crashes")) (map (:item "alert noise <2/day")) (map (:item "traffic migration 50%→99% completed")) (map (:item "Rust graceful drain, no 5xx")) (map (:item "100% cutover, cljc pool live, Rust shutdown"))))

  (:adr/performance-budgets "[{:metric \"p50 latency\" :phase-1-ms 80 :phase-2-ms 70 :phase-3-ms 70 :note \"baseline ~60ms\"} {:metric \"p95 latency\" :phase-1-ms 120 :phase-2-ms 95 :phase-3-ms 95 :note \"accept 5% variance in ramp\"} {:metric \"p99 latency\" :phase-1-ms 150 :phase-2-ms 100 :phase-3-ms 100 :note \"hard budget\"} {:metric \"throughput loss %\" :phase-1-pct 2 :phase-2-pct 1 :phase-3-pct 0 :note \"vs baseline\"} {:metric \"JVM heap peak MB\" :phase-1-mb 256 :phase-2-mb 384 :phase-3-mb 256 :note \"post-GC stable\"} {:metric \"GC pause p99\" :phase-1-ms 50 :phase-2-ms 30 :phase-3-ms 30 :note \"ZGC/Shenandoah\"} {:metric \"parity failure rate %\" :phase-1-pct 0.01 :phase-2-pct 0.05 :phase-3-pct 0.01 :note \"content-hash mismatch\"} {:metric \"HTTP 5xx rate %\" :phase-1-pct 0.01 :phase-2-pct 0.1 :phase-3-pct 0.01 :note \"unhandled exceptions\"}]")

